# FatFs on Linux

Linux's own FatFs: ChaN's R0.16 archive, which vendor.sh fetches, checks
against its pinned SHA-256, and unpacks into upstream/; the project's
ffconf.h, forced into every file with -include so the checkout is never
edited; the project-owned adapter.c over it; and platform.linux.fs.fat, the
provider the Linux SDKs bind for mm.fs.fat. mm.build compiles ff.c,
ffunicode.c, and the adapter -- the adapter with warnings as errors -- for a
program that reaches the provider, and links them into it.

It is independent of the Pico path, platforms/pico/sdk/pico-sdk/fatfs, which
the Pico SDK bridge compiles: its own archive, configuration, adapter, and
provider, so either can change without the other. Both start at R0.16 with
the same configuration; mm.fs.conformance checks both against one contract.
The adapter's ABI is prefixed mm_linux_fat_ where the Pico one's is
mm_pico_fat_.
